Landon Rusco is an undergraduate student at SUNY Oswego studying Software Engineering. He is the sole Web Developer of the official SOAC website, and the genius engineer behind the SOACWebEdit project, which is a Java desktop application geared towards enabling non-web-designers to seamlessly use generative AI to edit and improve the SOAC website as it continues to grow and flourish with its organization.
He was the President of the Oswego Computer Science Association, and one of few Co-founders of the interstate Hackathon LakerHacks held annually at Oswego. As a full-stack software engineer, he prides himself on his many educational, professional, and auxillary programming projects he's posted on his GitHub, as well as his extensive unix system expertise.
During his free time, he practices shotokan karate, woodcarving, and steel-forging.